176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (The Water Footprint Network estimates that producing printing and writing paper requires approximately 2 to 13 litres of supply-chain water per A4 sheet, depending on factors such as the paper source, recycled content, paper type, and manufacturing process. This water footprint includes water used in forestry, pulp production, and paper manufacturing, rather than only water used at the printing shop. Based on this estimate, producing 5,000 sheets of paper could require approximately 10,000 to 65,000 litres of water, while producing 15,000 sheets could require approximately 30,000 to 195,000 litres. Therefore, the estimated overall supply-chain water footprint of printing 5,000 to 15,000 pages is approximately 10,000 to 195,000 litres per semester.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
