>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (The TO-BE model presents the proposed paperless Capstone C submission process through a Digital Capstone Repository. The student logs in using an EWU Gmail account, enters the required project information, and uploads one final thesis PDF. The system automatically checks the file format and metadata. If any error is detected, the student receives an error message, corrects the report, and resubmits it digitally.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (After successful validation, the report is sent to the supervisor for online review. The supervisor can approve the report or reject it with comments. When rejected, the student receives the feedback, makes the required corrections, and submits the revised report through the same system.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (Once approved, the system locks the verified PDF, assigns a unique report ID, records the submission date and time, generates a file hash, and stores the report securely. The student then receives an acceptance notification, and the approved report becomes accessible to authorized EWU Gmail users.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (This redesigned process removes compulsory printing, binding, travel, and physical storage. It reduces paper waste, waiting time, printing errors, student costs, and environmental impact while improving report verification, accessibility, preservation, and administrative efficiency.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
