<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (A Bangladesh-hosted 20 GB advanced hosting package would cost approximately BDT 12,000 per year. The package includes free SSL, SSH access, and up to seven days of daily backups. EWU could use a university subdomain, such as capstone.ewubd.edu, which would remove the need to purchase a separate domain.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Over five years, the total cost of ownership would depend on both the initial development cost and the selected maintenance level. With an initial development cost of BDT 400,000, the estimated five-year cost ranges from BDT 460,000 when no separate maintenance cost is included to BDT 1,060,000 when annual maintenance is BDT 120,000. With an initial development cost of BDT 1,500,000, the estimated five-year cost ranges from BDT 1,560,000 to BDT 2,160,000 under the same maintenance scenarios. These figures show that the repository requires a significant initial investment, but it provides a long-term institutional system for secure submission, approval, storage, retrieval, and preservation of Capstone reports.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (ESTIMATED COST OF IMPLEMENTING THE TO-BE MODEL)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (The proposed Digital Capstone Repository would require an estimated development cost of approximately BDT 400,000 to BDT 1,500,000. This is considered a reasonable production-level estimate for a medium-complexity system containing role-based permissions, automated workflows, reporting features, and external integrations. A student prototype could be developed at a lower cost, but it would not provide the same level of security, reliability, scalability, testing, and technical support required for an official university system.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (ENVIRONMENTAL FOOTPRINT)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (The environmental footprint calculation assumes that the Digital Capstone Repository operates continuously for one four-month semester, equivalent to approximately 2,920 hours. The repository is assumed to use one continuously running virtual CPU and 20 GB, or 0.02 TB, of SSD storage. A Power Usage Effectiveness value of 1.25 is used to account for cooling, lighting, power conversion, and other data-centre overhead. This value was selected as a reasonable conservative assumption )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
