<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (This graph compares the electricity use of the two processes. Active printing consumes about 1.27 to 3.81 kWh per semester, while the digital repository is estimated to use about 7.78 kWh because it operates continuously and includes data-centre overhead. Therefore, the repository does not reduce electricity use by itself. However, it is greener overall because it avoids the much larger impacts of paper production, printing, binding, reprinting, and student travel.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
